A cluster is a fully managed Kubernetes cluster
It is composed of different pools, each pool containing the same kind of nodes.

USAGE:
  scw k8s cluster <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  cockpit                 Open the Cockpit Grafana dashboard for this cluster
  connect                 Connect to a cluster using k9s, or a custom command via template
  create                  Create a new Cluster
  delete                  Delete a Cluster
  get                     Get a Cluster
  list                    List Clusters
  list-available-types    List available cluster types for a cluster
  list-available-versions List available versions for a Cluster
  reset-admin-token       Reset the admin token of a Cluster
  set-type                Change the Cluster type
  update                  Update a Cluster
  upgrade                 Upgrade a Cluster

WORKFLOW COMMANDS:
  wait                    Wait for a cluster to reach a stable state

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for cluster
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw k8s cluster [command] --help" for more information about a command.
